"Show Tips Weekly" = "Show Tips Weekly";
"Show Tips Daily" = "Show Tips Daily";
"Share" = "Share";
"iTerm2 Tip of the Day" = "iTerm2 Tip of the Day";
"Tip of the Day" = "Tip of the Day";
"This window shows the iTerm2 tip of the day. It’ll appear every 24 hours to let you know about new features and hidden secrets. Hit “More Options” to view more tips or to stop getting them altogether." = "This window shows the iTerm2 tip of the day. It’ll appear every 24 hours to let you know about new features and hidden secrets. Hit “More Options” to view more tips or to stop getting them altogether.";
"Shell Integration" = "Shell Integration";
"The big new feature of iTerm2 version 3 is Shell Integration. Click “Learn More” for all the details." = "The big new feature of iTerm2 version 3 is Shell Integration. Click “Learn More” for all the details.";
"Timestamps" = "Timestamps";
"“View > Show Timestamps” shows the time (and date, if appropriate) when each line was last modified." = "“View > Show Timestamps” shows the time (and date, if appropriate) when each line was last modified.";
"Password Manager" = "Password Manager";
"Did you know iTerm2 has a password manager? Open it with “Window > Password Manager.” You can define a Trigger to open it for you at a password prompt in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Triggers.”" = "Did you know iTerm2 has a password manager? Open it with “Window > Password Manager.” You can define a Trigger to open it for you at a password prompt in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Triggers.”";
"Open Quickly" = "Open Quickly";
"You can quickly search through your sessions with “View > Open Quickly” (⇧⌘O). You can type a query and sessions whose name, badge, current hostname, current user name, recent commands, and recent working directories match will be surfaced. It works best with Shell Integration so the user name, hostname, command, and directories can be known even while sshed." = "You can quickly search through your sessions with “View > Open Quickly” (⇧⌘O). You can type a query and sessions whose name, badge, current hostname, current user name, recent commands, and recent working directories match will be surfaced. It works best with Shell Integration so the user name, hostname, command, and directories can be known even while sshed.";
"Undo Close" = "Undo Close";
"If you close a session, tab, or window by accident you can undo it with “Edit > Undo” (⌘Z). By default you have five seconds to undo, but you can adjust that timeout in “Settings > Profiles > Session.”" = "If you close a session, tab, or window by accident you can undo it with “Edit > Undo” (⌘Z). By default you have five seconds to undo, but you can adjust that timeout in “Settings > Profiles > Session.”";
"Annotations" = "Annotations";
"Want to mark up your scrollback history? Right click on a selection and choose “Annotate Selection” to add a personal note to it. Use “View > Show Annotations” to show or hide them, and look in “Edit > Marks and Annotations” for more things you can do." = "Want to mark up your scrollback history? Right click on a selection and choose “Annotate Selection” to add a personal note to it. Use “View > Show Annotations” to show or hide them, and look in “Edit > Marks and Annotations” for more things you can do.";
"Copy with Styles" = "Copy with Styles";
"Copy a selection with ⌥⌘C to include styles such as colors and fonts. You can make this the default action for Copy in “Settings > Advanced.”" = "Copy a selection with ⌥⌘C to include styles such as colors and fonts. You can make this the default action for Copy in “Settings > Advanced.”";
"Inline Images" = "Inline Images";
"iTerm2 can display images (even animated GIFs) inline." = "iTerm2 can display images (even animated GIFs) inline.";
"Automatic Profile Switching" = "Automatic Profile Switching";
"Automatic Profile Switching changes the current profile when the username, hostname, or directory changes. Set it up in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced.” It requires Shell Integration to be installed." = "Automatic Profile Switching changes the current profile when the username, hostname, or directory changes. Set it up in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced.” It requires Shell Integration to be installed.";
"Captured Output" = "Captured Output";
"iTerm2 can act like an IDE using the Captured Output feature. When it sees text matching a regular expression you define, like compiler errors, it shows the matching lines in the Toolbelt. You can click to jump to the line in your terminal and double-click to perform an action like opening an editor to the line with the error." = "iTerm2 can act like an IDE using the Captured Output feature. When it sees text matching a regular expression you define, like compiler errors, it shows the matching lines in the Toolbelt. You can click to jump to the line in your terminal and double-click to perform an action like opening an editor to the line with the error.";
"Badges" = "Badges";
"You can display a status message in the top right of your session in the background. It’s called a “Badge.” If you install Shell Integration you can include info like user name, hostname, current directory, and more." = "You can display a status message in the top right of your session in the background. It’s called a “Badge.” If you install Shell Integration you can include info like user name, hostname, current directory, and more.";
"Dynamic Profiles" = "Dynamic Profiles";
"Dynamic Profiles let you store your profiles as one or more JSON files. It’s great for batch creating and editing profiles." = "Dynamic Profiles let you store your profiles as one or more JSON files. It’s great for batch creating and editing profiles.";
"Advanced Paste" = "Advanced Paste";
"“Edit > Paste Special > Advanced Paste” lets you preview and edit text before you paste. You get to tweak options, like how to handle control codes, or even to base-64 encode before pasting." = "“Edit > Paste Special > Advanced Paste” lets you preview and edit text before you paste. You get to tweak options, like how to handle control codes, or even to base-64 encode before pasting.";
"Zoom" = "Zoom";
"Ever wanted to focus on a block of lines without distraction, or limit Find to a single command’s output? Select the lines and choose “View > Zoom In on Selection.” The session’s contents will be temporarily replaced with the selection. Press “esc” to unzoom." = "Ever wanted to focus on a block of lines without distraction, or limit Find to a single command’s output? Select the lines and choose “View > Zoom In on Selection.” The session’s contents will be temporarily replaced with the selection. Press “esc” to unzoom.";
"Semantic History" = "Semantic History";
"The “Semantic History” feature allows you to ⌘-click on a file or URL to open it." = "The “Semantic History” feature allows you to ⌘-click on a file or URL to open it.";
"Tmux Integration" = "Tmux Integration";
"If you use tmux, try running “tmux -CC” to get iTerm2’s tmux integration mode. The tmux windows show up as native iTerm2 windows, and you can use iTerm2’s keyboard shortcuts. It even works over ssh!" = "If you use tmux, try running “tmux -CC” to get iTerm2’s tmux integration mode. The tmux windows show up as native iTerm2 windows, and you can use iTerm2’s keyboard shortcuts. It even works over ssh!";
"Triggers" = "Triggers";
"iTerm2 can automatically perform actions you define when text matching a regular expression is received. For example, you can highlight text or show an alert box. Set it up in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Triggers.”" = "iTerm2 can automatically perform actions you define when text matching a regular expression is received. For example, you can highlight text or show an alert box. Set it up in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Triggers.”";
"Smart Selection" = "Smart Selection";
"Quadruple click to perform Smart Selection. It figures out if you’re selecting a URL, filename, email address, etc. based on prioritized regular expressions." = "Quadruple click to perform Smart Selection. It figures out if you’re selecting a URL, filename, email address, etc. based on prioritized regular expressions.";
"Instant Replay" = "Instant Replay";
"Press ⌥⌘B to step back in time in a terminal window. Use arrow keys to go frame by frame. Hold ⇧ and press arrow keys to go faster." = "Press ⌥⌘B to step back in time in a terminal window. Use arrow keys to go frame by frame. Hold ⇧ and press arrow keys to go faster.";
"Hotkey Window" = "Hotkey Window";
"You can have a terminal window open with a keystroke, even while in other apps. Click “Create a Dedicated Hotkey Window” in “Settings > Keys.”" = "You can have a terminal window open with a keystroke, even while in other apps. Click “Create a Dedicated Hotkey Window” in “Settings > Keys.”";
"Hotkey windows can stay open after losing focus. Turn it on in “Window > Pin Hotkey Window.”" = "Hotkey windows can stay open after losing focus. Turn it on in “Window > Pin Hotkey Window.”";
"Cursor Guide" = "Cursor Guide";
"The cursor guide is a horizontal line that follows your cursor. You can turn it on in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” or toggle it with the ⌥⌘; shortcut." = "The cursor guide is a horizontal line that follows your cursor. You can turn it on in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” or toggle it with the ⌥⌘; shortcut.";
"Shell Integration: Alerts" = "Shell Integration: Alerts";
"The Shell Integration feature lets you ask to be alerted (⌥⌘A) when a long-running command completes." = "The Shell Integration feature lets you ask to be alerted (⌥⌘A) when a long-running command completes.";
"Cursor Blink Rate" = "Cursor Blink Rate";
"You can configure how quickly the cursor blinks in “Settings > Advanced.”" = "You can configure how quickly the cursor blinks in “Settings > Advanced.”";
"Shell Integration: Navigation" = "Shell Integration: Navigation";
"The Shell Integration feature lets you navigate among shell prompts with ⇧⌘↑ and ⇧⌘↓." = "The Shell Integration feature lets you navigate among shell prompts with ⇧⌘↑ and ⇧⌘↓.";
"Shell Integration: Status" = "Shell Integration: Status";
"The Shell Integration feature puts a blue arrow next to your shell prompt. If you run a command that fails, it turns red. Right click on it to get the running time and status." = "The Shell Integration feature puts a blue arrow next to your shell prompt. If you run a command that fails, it turns red. Right click on it to get the running time and status.";
"Shell Integration: Selection" = "Shell Integration: Selection";
"With Shell Integration installed, you can select the output of the last command with ⇧⌘A." = "With Shell Integration installed, you can select the output of the last command with ⇧⌘A.";
"Bells" = "Bells";
"The dock icon shows a count of the number of bells rung and notifications posted since the app was last active." = "The dock icon shows a count of the number of bells rung and notifications posted since the app was last active.";
"Shell Integration: Downloads" = "Shell Integration: Downloads";
"If you install Shell Integration on a machine you ssh to, you can right click on a filename (for example, in the output of “ls”) and choose “Download with scp” to download the file." = "If you install Shell Integration on a machine you ssh to, you can right click on a filename (for example, in the output of “ls”) and choose “Download with scp” to download the file.";
"Find Your Cursor" = "Find Your Cursor";
"Press ⌘/ to locate your cursor. It’s fun!" = "Press ⌘/ to locate your cursor. It’s fun!";
"Customize Smart Selection" = "Customize Smart Selection";
"You can edit Smart Selection regular expressions in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Smart Selection.”" = "You can edit Smart Selection regular expressions in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Smart Selection.”";
"Smart Selection Actions" = "Smart Selection Actions";
"Assign an action to a Smart Selection rule in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Smart Selection > Edit Actions.” They go in the context menu and override semantic history on ⌘-click." = "Assign an action to a Smart Selection rule in “Settings > Profiles > Advanced > Smart Selection > Edit Actions.” They go in the context menu and override semantic history on ⌘-click.";
"Visual Bell" = "Visual Bell";
"If you want the visual bell to flash the whole screen instead of show a bell icon, you can turn that on in “Settings > Advanced.”" = "If you want the visual bell to flash the whole screen instead of show a bell icon, you can turn that on in “Settings > Advanced.”";
"Tab Menu" = "Tab Menu";
"Right click on a tab to change its color, close tabs after it, or to close all other tabs." = "Right click on a tab to change its color, close tabs after it, or to close all other tabs.";
"Tags" = "Tags";
"You can assign tags to your profiles, and by clicking “Tags>” anywhere you see a list of profiles you can browse those tags." = "You can assign tags to your profiles, and by clicking “Tags>” anywhere you see a list of profiles you can browse those tags.";
"Tag Hierarchy" = "Tag Hierarchy";
"If you put a slash in a profile’s tag, that implicitly defines a hierarchy. You can see it in the Profiles menu as nested submenus." = "If you put a slash in a profile’s tag, that implicitly defines a hierarchy. You can see it in the Profiles menu as nested submenus.";
"Downloads" = "Downloads";
"iTerm2 can download files by base-64 encoding them. Click “Learn More” to download a shell script that makes it easy." = "iTerm2 can download files by base-64 encoding them. Click “Learn More” to download a shell script that makes it easy.";
"Command Completion" = "Command Completion";
"If you install Shell Integration, ⇧⌘; helps you complete commands. It remembers the commands you’ve run on each host that has Shell Integration installed. It knows how often that command was run and how recently to help make the best suggestions." = "If you install Shell Integration, ⇧⌘; helps you complete commands. It remembers the commands you’ve run on each host that has Shell Integration installed. It knows how often that command was run and how recently to help make the best suggestions.";
"Recent Directories" = "Recent Directories";
"iTerm2 remembers which directories you use the most on each host that has Shell Integration installed. There’s a Toolbelt tool to browse them, and ⌥⌘/ gives you a popup sorted by frequency and recency of use." = "iTerm2 remembers which directories you use the most on each host that has Shell Integration installed. There’s a Toolbelt tool to browse them, and ⌥⌘/ gives you a popup sorted by frequency and recency of use.";
"Favorite Directories" = "Favorite Directories";
"If you have Shell Integration installed, you can “star” a directory to keep it always at the bottom of the Recent Directories tool in the Toolbelt. Right click and choose “Toggle Star.”" = "If you have Shell Integration installed, you can “star” a directory to keep it always at the bottom of the Recent Directories tool in the Toolbelt. Right click and choose “Toggle Star.”";
"Shell Integration History" = "Shell Integration History";
"Install Shell Integration and turn on “Settings > General > Save copy/paste and command history to disk” to remember command history per host across restarts of iTerm2." = "Install Shell Integration and turn on “Settings > General > Save copy/paste and command history to disk” to remember command history per host across restarts of iTerm2.";
"Paste File as Base64" = "Paste File as Base64";
"Copy a file to the pasteboard in Finder and then use “Edit > Paste Special > Paste File Base64-Encoded” for easy uploads of binary files. Use ”base64 -D” (or -d on Linux) on the remote host to decode it." = "Copy a file to the pasteboard in Finder and then use “Edit > Paste Special > Paste File Base64-Encoded” for easy uploads of binary files. Use ”base64 -D” (or -d on Linux) on the remote host to decode it.";
"Split Panes" = "Split Panes";
"You can split a tab into multiple panes with ⌘D and ⇧⌘D." = "You can split a tab into multiple panes with ⌘D and ⇧⌘D.";
"Adjust Split Panes" = "Adjust Split Panes";
"Resize split panes with the keyboard using ^⌘-Arrow Key." = "Resize split panes with the keyboard using ^⌘-Arrow Key.";
"Move Cursor" = "Move Cursor";
"Hold ⌥ and click to move your cursor. It works best with Shell Integration installed (to avoid sending up/down arrow keys to your shell)." = "Hold ⌥ and click to move your cursor. It works best with Shell Integration installed (to avoid sending up/down arrow keys to your shell).";
"Edge Windows" = "Edge Windows";
"You can tell your profile to create windows that are attached to one edge of the screen in “Settings > Profiles > Window.” You can resize them by dragging the edges." = "You can tell your profile to create windows that are attached to one edge of the screen in “Settings > Profiles > Window.” You can resize them by dragging the edges.";
"Tab Color" = "Tab Color";
"You can assign colors to tabs in “Settings > Profiles > Colors,” or in the View menu." = "You can assign colors to tabs in “Settings > Profiles > Colors,” or in the View menu.";
"Rectangular Selection" = "Rectangular Selection";
"Hold ⌥⌘ while dragging to make a rectangular selection." = "Hold ⌥⌘ while dragging to make a rectangular selection.";
"Multiple Selection" = "Multiple Selection";
"Hold ⌘ while dragging to make multiple discontinuous selections." = "Hold ⌘ while dragging to make multiple discontinuous selections.";
"Dragging Panes" = "Dragging Panes";
"Hold ⇧⌥⌘ and drag a session into another session to create or change split panes." = "Hold ⇧⌥⌘ and drag a session into another session to create or change split panes.";
"Cursor Boost" = "Cursor Boost";
"Adjust Cursor Boost in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” to make all colors more muted, except the cursor. Use a bright white cursor and it pops!" = "Adjust Cursor Boost in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” to make all colors more muted, except the cursor. Use a bright white cursor and it pops!";
"Minimum Contrast" = "Minimum Contrast";
"Adjust “Minimum Contrast” in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” to ensure text is always legible regardless of text/background color combination." = "Adjust “Minimum Contrast” in “Settings > Profiles > Colors” to ensure text is always legible regardless of text/background color combination.";
"Tabs" = "Tabs";
"Normally, new tabs appear at the end of the tab bar. There’s a setting in “Settings > Advanced” to place them next to your current tab." = "Normally, new tabs appear at the end of the tab bar. There’s a setting in “Settings > Advanced” to place them next to your current tab.";
"Base Conversion" = "Base Conversion";
"Right-click on a number and the context menu shows it converted to hex or decimal as appropriate." = "Right-click on a number and the context menu shows it converted to hex or decimal as appropriate.";
"Saved Searches" = "Saved Searches";
"In “Settings > Keys” you can assign a keystroke to a search for a regular expression with the “Find Regular Expression…” action." = "In “Settings > Keys” you can assign a keystroke to a search for a regular expression with the “Find Regular Expression…” action.";
"Find URLs" = "Find URLs";
"Search for URLs using “Edit > Find > Find URLs.” Navigate search results with ⌘G and ⇧⌘G. Open the current selection with ⌥⌘O." = "Search for URLs using “Edit > Find > Find URLs.” Navigate search results with ⌘G and ⇧⌘G. Open the current selection with ⌥⌘O.";
"The “instant” checkbox in a Trigger allows it to fire while the cursor is on the same line as the text that matches your regular expression." = "The “instant” checkbox in a Trigger allows it to fire while the cursor is on the same line as the text that matches your regular expression.";
"Soft Boundaries" = "Soft Boundaries";
"Turn on “Edit > Selection Respects Soft Boundaries” to recognize split pane dividers in programs like vi, emacs, and tmux so you can select multiple lines of text." = "Turn on “Edit > Selection Respects Soft Boundaries” to recognize split pane dividers in programs like vi, emacs, and tmux so you can select multiple lines of text.";
"Select Without Dragging" = "Select Without Dragging";
"Single click where you want to start a selection and ⇧-click where you want it to end to select text without dragging." = "Single click where you want to start a selection and ⇧-click where you want it to end to select text without dragging.";
"Smooth Window Resizing" = "Smooth Window Resizing";
"Hold ^ while resizing a window and it won’t snap to the character grid: you can make it any size you want." = "Hold ^ while resizing a window and it won’t snap to the character grid: you can make it any size you want.";
"Pasting Tabs" = "Pasting Tabs";
"If you paste text containing tabs, you’ll be asked if you want to convert them to spaces. It’s handy at the shell prompt to avoid triggering filename completion." = "If you paste text containing tabs, you’ll be asked if you want to convert them to spaces. It’s handy at the shell prompt to avoid triggering filename completion.";
"Bell Silencing" = "Bell Silencing";
"Did you know? If the bell rings too often, you’ll be asked if you’d like to silence it temporarily. iTerm2 cares about your comfort." = "Did you know? If the bell rings too often, you’ll be asked if you’d like to silence it temporarily. iTerm2 cares about your comfort.";
"Profile Search" = "Profile Search";
"Every list of profiles has a search field (e.g., in ”Settings > Profiles.”) You can use various operators to restrict your search query. Click “Learn More” for all the details." = "Every list of profiles has a search field (e.g., in ”Settings > Profiles.”) You can use various operators to restrict your search query. Click “Learn More” for all the details.";
"Color Schemes" = "Color Schemes";
"The online color gallery features over one hundred beautiful color schemes you can download." = "The online color gallery features over one hundred beautiful color schemes you can download.";
"ASCII/Non-Ascii Fonts" = "ASCII/Non-Ascii Fonts";
"You can have a separate font for ASCII versus non-ASCII text. Enable it in “Settings > Profiles > Text.”" = "You can have a separate font for ASCII versus non-ASCII text. Enable it in “Settings > Profiles > Text.”";
"Coprocesses" = "Coprocesses";
"A coprocess is a job, such as a shell script, that has a special relationship with a particular iTerm2 session. All output in a terminal window (that is, what you see on the screen) is also input to the coprocess. All output from the coprocess acts like text that the user is typing at the keyboard." = "A coprocess is a job, such as a shell script, that has a special relationship with a particular iTerm2 session. All output in a terminal window (that is, what you see on the screen) is also input to the coprocess. All output from the coprocess acts like text that the user is typing at the keyboard.";
"Touch Bar Customization" = "Touch Bar Customization";
"You can customize the touch bar by selecting “View > Customize Touch Bar.” You can add a tab bar for full-screen mode, a user-customizable status button, and you can even define your own touch bar buttons in Settings > Keys. There’s also a new shell integration tool to customize touch bar function key labels." = "You can customize the touch bar by selecting “View > Customize Touch Bar.” You can add a tab bar for full-screen mode, a user-customizable status button, and you can even define your own touch bar buttons in Settings > Keys. There’s also a new shell integration tool to customize touch bar function key labels.";
"Ligatures" = "Ligatures";
"If you use a font that supports ligatures, you can enable ligature support in Settings > Profiles > Text." = "If you use a font that supports ligatures, you can enable ligature support in Settings > Profiles > Text.";
"Floating Hotkey Window" = "Floating Hotkey Window";
"New in 3.1: You can configure your hotkey window to appear over other apps’ full screen windows. Turn on “Floating Window” in “Settings > Profiles > Keys > Customize Hotkey Window.”" = "New in 3.1: You can configure your hotkey window to appear over other apps’ full screen windows. Turn on “Floating Window” in “Settings > Profiles > Keys > Customize Hotkey Window.”";
"Multiple Hotkey Windows" = "Multiple Hotkey Windows";
"New in 3.1: You can have multiple hotkey windows. Each profile can have one or more hotkeys." = "New in 3.1: You can have multiple hotkey windows. Each profile can have one or more hotkeys.";
"Double-Tap Hotkey" = "Double-Tap Hotkey";
"New in 3.1: You can configure a hotkey window to open on double-tap of a modifier in “Settings > Profiles > Keys > Customize Hotkey Window.”" = "New in 3.1: You can configure a hotkey window to open on double-tap of a modifier in “Settings > Profiles > Keys > Customize Hotkey Window.”";
"Buried Sessions" = "Buried Sessions";
"You can “bury” a session with “Session > Bury Session.” It remains hidden until you restore it by selecting it from “Session > Buried Sessions > Your session.”" = "You can “bury” a session with “Session > Bury Session.” It remains hidden until you restore it by selecting it from “Session > Buried Sessions > Your session.”";
"Python API" = "Python API";
"You can add custom behavior to iTerm2 using the Python API." = "You can add custom behavior to iTerm2 using the Python API.";
"Status Bar" = "Status Bar";
"You can add a configurable status bar to your terminal windows." = "You can add a configurable status bar to your terminal windows.";
"Minimal Theme" = "Minimal Theme";
"Try the “Minimal” and “Compact” themes to reduce visual clutter. You can set it in “Settings > Appearance > General.”" = "Try the “Minimal” and “Compact” themes to reduce visual clutter. You can set it in “Settings > Appearance > General.”";
"Session Titles" = "Session Titles";
"You can configure which elements are present in session titles in “Settings > Profiles > General > Title.”" = "You can configure which elements are present in session titles in “Settings > Profiles > General > Title.”";
"Tab Icons" = "Tab Icons";
"Tabs can show an icon indicating the current application. Configure it in “Settings > Profiles > General > Icon.”" = "Tabs can show an icon indicating the current application. Configure it in “Settings > Profiles > General > Icon.”";
"Drag Window by Tab" = "Drag Window by Tab";
"Hold ⌥ while dragging a tab to move the window. This is useful in the Compact and Minimal themes, which have a very small area for dragging the window." = "Hold ⌥ while dragging a tab to move the window. This is useful in the Compact and Minimal themes, which have a very small area for dragging the window.";
"Composer" = "Composer";
"Press ⇧⌘. to open the Composer. It gives you a scratchpad to edit a command before sending it to the shell." = "Press ⇧⌘. to open the Composer. It gives you a scratchpad to edit a command before sending it to the shell.";
"Shell Integration: Uploads" = "Shell Integration: Uploads";
"If you install Shell Integration on a machine you ssh to, you can drag-drop from Finder into the remote host by holding ⌥ while dragging. The destination directory is determined by where you drop the file in the terminal window: run cd foo, then drop the file below the cd command, and the file will go into the foo directory." = "If you install Shell Integration on a machine you ssh to, you can drag-drop from Finder into the remote host by holding ⌥ while dragging. The destination directory is determined by where you drop the file in the terminal window: run cd foo, then drop the file below the cd command, and the file will go into the foo directory.";
"Composer Power Features" = "Composer Power Features";
"The composer supports multiple cursors. It also has the ability to send just one command out of a list, making it easy to walk through a list of commands one-by-one. Click the help button in the composer for details." = "The composer supports multiple cursors. It also has the ability to send just one command out of a list, making it easy to walk through a list of commands one-by-one. Click the help button in the composer for details.";
"Render Selection" = "Render Selection";
"Transform selected text into a prettified, syntax-highlighted view with the “Render Selection” command, ideal for JSON, Markdown, or source code. This feature includes horizontal scrolling for easy log navigation." = "Transform selected text into a prettified, syntax-highlighted view with the “Render Selection” command, ideal for JSON, Markdown, or source code. This feature includes horizontal scrolling for easy log navigation.";
"SSH Integration" = "SSH Integration";
"Export environment variables and copy files to remote hosts seamlessly with SSH integration. Either configure a profile to use ssh or use it2ssh in place of ssh." = "Export environment variables and copy files to remote hosts seamlessly with SSH integration. Either configure a profile to use ssh or use it2ssh in place of ssh.";
"Auto Composer" = "Auto Composer";
"Improve your command line with the “auto composer”, which replaces the command line with a native control for ease of use. Requires shell integration." = "Improve your command line with the “auto composer”, which replaces the command line with a native control for ease of use. Requires shell integration.";
"AI Command Writing" = "AI Command Writing";
"Generate commands using AI by entering a prompt in the composer and selecting “Edit > Engage Artificial Intelligence”. An OpenAI API key is required for this functionality." = "Generate commands using AI by entering a prompt in the composer and selecting “Edit > Engage Artificial Intelligence”. An OpenAI API key is required for this functionality.";
"Codecierge Tool" = "Codecierge Tool";
"Set and achieve terminal goals with “Codecierge”, a Toolbelt feature that guides you step-by-step based on your terminal activity. An OpenAI API key is necessary for this feature." = "Set and achieve terminal goals with “Codecierge”, a Toolbelt feature that guides you step-by-step based on your terminal activity. An OpenAI API key is necessary for this feature.";
"Named Marks" = "Named Marks";
"Navigate your command history effortlessly with “named marks” by assigning names to lines in the terminal." = "Navigate your command history effortlessly with “named marks” by assigning names to lines in the terminal.";
"Font Assignments" = "Font Assignments";
"You can assign specific fonts to Unicode ranges. Use 'Settings > Profiles > Text > Manage Special Exceptions' to manage it and to install a huge set of Powerline symbols." = "You can assign specific fonts to Unicode ranges. Use 'Settings > Profiles > Text > Manage Special Exceptions' to manage it and to install a huge set of Powerline symbols.";
